WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.060
Picture a strawberry farm.

2
00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.200
When the price of strawberries rises,

3
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.610
the farmer offers more for sale.

4
00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:11.280
In July 2021, frosts hit
coffee-growing areas of Brazil,

5
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.670
the world's largest coffee producer.

6
00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.620
Damaged trees meant less coffee
for sale in later harvests.

7
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.930
No change in price caused this.

8
00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.160
So why do farmers grow
more when prices rise,

9
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.060
and what makes them grow
less at every price?

10
00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:28.840
In this mission, you'll
build a supply curve and see

11
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.610
why it slopes upwards.

12
00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.130
Then you'll add a tax,

13
00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.130
change costs and add
firms in the graph lab,

14
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.120
and predict what the curve does.

15
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.910
Your mission: explain what moves
a producer along the curve,

16
00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.680
and what moves the curve itself.
